    "sha": "779f1ae81f196f56c6d3f2db7fe832ccda8c3266",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOMVotWtoAKDc3OWYxYWU4MWYxOTZmNTZjNmQzZjJkYjdmZTgzMmNjZGE4YzMyNjY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Paul A. Clarke",
        "email": "paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com",
        "date": "2026-04-11T14:51:04Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Paul A. Clarke",
        "email": "paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com",
        "date": "2026-04-15T15:02:45Z"
      },
      "message": "Add even more pseudoinstructions\n\nTwo particularly interesting cases:\n- Some vector \"less than or equal\"/\"greater than\" instructions are mapped to\n  \"less than\"/\"greater than or equal\" pseudoinstructions with the immediate\n  incremented. So, these need to allow for (by ignoring) cases where the\n  immediate cannot be incremented without overflowing.\n- `vmnot.v` depends on the immediate for `vxor.vi` being \"-1\", thus\n  sign-extended. Add this attribute to the opcode field (and presume the\n  attribute is applied before pseudoinstruction mapping).\n\nSigned-off-by: Paul A. Clarke <paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "bc450512298c1b4295e62874c6aadac3f79c7376",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-unified-db/git/trees/bc450512298c1b4295e62874c6aadac3f79c7376"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-unified-db/git/commits/779f1ae81f196f56c6d3f2db7fe832ccda8c3266",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAARUAAAAHc3NoLXJzYQAAAAEjAAABAQDGJ7b9OuWx+6Aewmy+pApQO2\nd3lVhQrDSCIx1LBls0DOBHCEcVs4RabvUoyDI6/OPXjNpYWcPTFwRr6Mo5czZ1mkNIv0Vn\nTprHTIAMc1jGUjeHBLPTbFx78rVedoM+wvfv98rUZL+LCyglMCtMikZs0PJ4qZBn3TQ9bn\nqEiP1kyrqQwKQVKLv3IxhuvQcI1RSdiiuuwhVxscoUJeh6Kf4wOGI+uPDQXma3zhVnu2fD\nf7hNYSxq8an/Y83xh1D/4zLdF3Qh+BRrKEqOYdFJya603mgS5P458oCNnaTCWUkZQ9mCV9\nmT5pHquZV2c9EMWmRLKXq4hLhNRUTmA/HQs4f9AAAAA2dpdAAAAAAAAAAGc2hhNTEyAAAB\nFAAAAAxyc2Etc2hhMi01MTIAAAEAiBeHM3nUJQva16/Xv8qT6oNoVnyBHaIvte3Qp37PMq\nE7rcqcQIevbCRi9bOwvZbMarUGSDXanvhXPOeOK7MemgKZ4A3HtqBLSwzqo89i5RPMkTVj\nL+n2QtQcd6/pfEKev+1WdhtM1xbfCjwd0F0SLr7lE2L0suXXRe45r39zziZ2cEMPcm4bt6\nKyTDOER3BBcBmwXjpU7G0lV4fl43aHPOfIJ4L2XtVuBsJg8fo3lwQnfugKp3eceni76xWp\n8GBBMhngX65/aSrKYWJhcz6M2h8hS17F9HPK90i7EmfgMn/Jv0PsC+uvCRoVQ3QE8aly0E\n9qfUxLiGMsEM/7eGwWLg==\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree bc450512298c1b4295e62874c6aadac3f79c7376\nparent 48274203f8550793fc93e88b748ecce013f31880\nauthor Paul A. Clarke <paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com> 1775919064 -0500\ncommitter Paul A. Clarke <paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com> 1776265365 -0500\n\nAdd even more pseudoinstructions\n\nTwo particularly interesting cases:\n- Some vector \"less than or equal\"/\"greater than\" instructions are mapped to\n  \"less than\"/\"greater than or equal\" pseudoinstructions with the immediate\n  incremented. So, these need to allow for (by ignoring) cases where the\n  immediate cannot be incremented without overflowing.\n- `vmnot.v` depends on the immediate for `vxor.vi` being \"-1\", thus\n  sign-extended. Add this attribute to the opcode field (and presume the\n  attribute is applied before pseudoinstruction mapping).\n\nSigned-off-by: Paul A. Clarke <paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com>\n",
